@up UP link: The **Indian Institute of Vegetable Research** (IIVR) at **Varanasi** bred **Kashi Lalima** (red okra) and many "Kashi" vegetable varieties. The **Indian Institute of Sugarcane Research** is at **Lucknow**, and UP is India's largest sugarcane producer.

@section 25.2 | Oils, Biofuels and Industrial Products

@q 48:6-8

**Peppermint** oil (menthol) is stored mainly in the **leaves**; UP (Barabanki, Badaun, Rampur) produces most of India's mint, and India leads the world in menthol. **Litmus** comes from **lichens** (Roccella). Silver and gold **nanoparticles** have been made with leaf extracts of the weed *Parthenium*.

@q 48:9-13

**Petro-crops** are plants rich in **hydrocarbons and lipids** that can replace petroleum. **Jatropha** (ratanjot) and **karanja** (*Pongamia*, a legume) yield non-edible oil for **biodiesel**. India's first biodiesel plant came up at **Kakinada** (Andhra Pradesh). The National Policy on Biofuels (2018) focuses on non-edible oils and waste.

@q 48:14-18

@table
Product | Source
**Chilgoza** | Seeds of the pine *Pinus gerardiana* (Kinnaur, Himachal)
**Caffeine** | **Tea and coffee** (also cola); the main stimulant in tea leaves
Theobromine | Cocoa
**Iodine** | **Seaweeds** (kelp)
Agar | Red seaweeds (Gelidium, Gracilaria)
**Tapa cloth** | Inner bark of the paper mulberry (family **Moraceae**)
**Rayon** | Regenerated **cellulose** from wood pulp (not starch)
@end

