@q 48:20

@qnote 48:20 | The source gives **(a) & (b)**: **asafoetida (hing)** is the dried resin (oleo-gum) tapped from the **stem base and the thick roots** of *Ferula* plants. India began growing its own hing at Lahaul-Spiti (Himachal) in 2020.

@q 48:21-25

**Neem** (*Azadirachta indica*; "margosa") gives **azadirachtin**, a natural insect repellent, and neem-coated urea. **Tulsi**'s healing value comes from **phenols (eugenol) and flavonoids**. **Oxytocin** is a hormone, **aspartame** a synthetic sweetener and **neoprene** a synthetic rubber. Beet gives sugar (sucrose); honey has glucose and fructose; cotton is cellulose; milk has lactose.

@section 25.4 | Medicinal and Drug Plants

@q 48:26-28

@src1 48:2
@one
In which part of the cinchona plant is quinine naturally found?
@ans Bark
@end

@table
Drug | Plant / origin | Use
**Quinine** | **Bark of cinchona** | Malaria (oldest drug); synthetic **chloroquine** replaced it
**Artemisinin** (artemether, **arteether**) | *Artemisia annua* (sweet wormwood), a **seed plant** | Malaria; Tu Youyou, Nobel 2015; arteether was developed by CDRI Lucknow
**Reserpine** | **Sarpagandha** (*Rauwolfia*) root | High blood pressure
Ashwagandha (*Withania*) | Root | Tonic
**Morphine**, codeine, **noscapine** | **Opium poppy** latex | Pain (morphine), cough (noscapine)
**Heroin** | Made from **morphine** | Illegal narcotic
Taxol | Himalayan yew bark | Cancer
Ephedrine | *Ephedra* | Asthma
@end

@pyq U.P. R.O./A.R.O. (Mains) 2016
Hydroxychloroquine drug used for the treatment of CORONA patients is obtained from the bark of which of the following plants?
(a) Aswagandha
(b) Sarpagandha
(c) Cinchona
(d) Aloe vera
@ans (*)
@note **Hydroxychloroquine** is a fully **synthetic** drug; it is modelled on **quinine**, which comes from **cinchona** bark, but it is not extracted from any plant. The source therefore marks the question (*), with (c) as the intended link.
@end
@src 48:29

@q 48:30-33

**Opium** is the dried **latex of the unripe capsule** of *Papaver somniferum*, obtained by cutting the green pods. **Morphine** (about 10%) is its chief alkaloid. India is one of the few licensed opium growers (Madhya Pradesh, Rajasthan and **UP**, under the Narcotics Commissioner, Gwalior); the Government Opium and Alkaloid Works is at **Ghazipur** (UP).

@trap
**Kanchan = amla**, **Kashi Lalima = okra**, **Co 1148 = sugarcane**, **Jaya** = first dwarf rice of India. **Jatropha and karanja** are biodiesel plants. **Litmus from lichen**, **iodine from seaweed**, **chilgoza from pine**. **Opium = fruit latex**, **hing = stem and root resin**, **quinine = bark**, **rubber = stem latex**. **Heroin** comes from opium. **Hydroxychloroquine is synthetic.** Rayon is **cellulose**, not starch.
@end

